d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence, trafficking and exploitation;
e. allocating a budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence, trafficking and exploitation in accordance with regional financial capacity;
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence, trafficking and exploitation.
(2) In order to implement the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Mayor establishes programs and activities for action for the protection of women and children from trafficking and exploitation in one regional action plan as a basis for SKPD in implementing the protection of women and children from acts of violence, trafficking and exploitation.
