a. victim identification;
b. Legal assistance;
c. Medical rehabilitation;
d. Psychosocial rehabilitation;
e. Social reintegration;
f. Repatriation assistance;
g. Empowerment.
(5) Provision of women's protection services as referred to in paragraph (4), is borne by the Regional Government.

Article 7
(1) Guarantees for the protection of children's rights include:
a. Civil rights and freedoms;
b. basic welfare (education and health);
c. good care;
d. a safe and comfortable environment;
e. special protection for children with special needs;
f. the right to obtain appropriate information;
g. the right to assistance;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right to social rehabilitation;
j. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
k. the right of victims and their families to obtain ease in the judicial process;
l. the right to obtain protection facilities for children who do not have a place of residence and/or whose lives are threatened.
(2) Children with special needs as referred to in paragraph (1) letter e are:
a. children with physical disabilities;
b. children with intellectual disabilities;
c. children with visual impairments;
d. children with hearing and/or speech impairments;
e. children with multiple disabilities;
f. children with social-psychological problems.

