c. good care;
d. a safe and comfortable environment;
e. special protection for children with special needs;
f. the right to obtain appropriate information;
g. the right to assistance;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right to social rehabilitation;
j. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
k. the right of victims and their families to obtain ease in the judicial process;
l. the right to obtain protection facilities for children who do not have a place of residence and/or whose lives are threatened.
